<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #eaf2f8;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; padding: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Future Careers – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em; color: #333;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> Future Careers</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> I Want to Be a Doctor Because...</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Create a short narrative based on a personal experience. Interactive: Provide feedback on short texts during a peer review session.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a short description of their future career plans by listing their motivation and planned steps in sequence (e.g., "I want to be a doctor because I like helping people. First, I will study medicine. Next, I will gain experience by training at a hospital."). Can provide feedback on a peer's narrative about career plans (e.g., "Good job describing your future goals!"). Can clarify different job roles by writing simple descriptions supported with pictures for common tasks (e.g., "A doctor helps people get healthy.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays pictures of various professionals (doctor, lawyer, teacher, engineer, chef) and asks students to quickly write down one career they find interesting and one simple reason why, using "I want to be a... because..." (2-3 minutes).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes an example on the board: "I want to be a teacher because I like helping others." and orally models the use of "want to + infinitive." The teacher then points to the word "teacher" and asks, "What do I need to do to become a teacher?" and models writing "I will need to study at university." Emphasize pronunciation of modals 'will' and 'would' with sounds /ɪ/ and /ʊ/ respectively.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Am I talking about my job now, or my job in the future?" (Future)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does 'want to' express something I will definitely do, or something I wish/plan to do?" (Wish/Plan)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher will also clarify the pronunciation of /ʃ/ in "wish" and /tʃ/ in "teach" using a minimal pair activity.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Future Careers"</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short narrative excerpt (1-2 paragraphs) from a fictional teenager named Leo about his future career as a doctor, listing his motivation and planned steps. It includes target grammar (want to + infinitive, future tense, modals) and vocabulary (doctor, plan, study, internship, achieve, help, professional).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Example Text:</i><br>
                "My name is Leo, and I want to be a doctor. I would like to help people and make them healthy. First, I plan to study hard in high school to get good qualifications. Next, I will need to go to medical school for many years. After that, I would like to gain experience by doing an internship at a big hospital. I want to succeed and become a skilled and professional doctor. It is an important goal for me."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students demonstrate understanding of a short written narrative about future career plans by identifying key information.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (written):</b> Students read Leo's narrative and write short answers to the following questions:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What does Leo want to be?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Why does he want to be a doctor?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What is the first step he plans to take?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What kind of experience would he like to gain?</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Accuracy focus on Writing</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences using "want to + infinitive," future tense (will/plan to), and modals (would like to, need to), along with target vocabulary to express career goals and steps. Focus on sentence structure and clarity for writing short narratives.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1 (Controlled Writing - Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with incomplete sentences related to career plans. Students complete them using appropriate target grammar (want to + infinitive, will, would like to, need to) and vocabulary words. Example: "I ___ to be a ____ because I ___ helping people. First, I ___ study at university. Next, I ___ to find an ____." (want, doctor/teacher, like, will, need, internship)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2 (Semi-controlled Writing - Guided Sentence Construction):</b> Students work individually. The teacher gives prompts for different careers (e.g., "Lawyer: help justice, study law, gain experience") and students write 2-3 sentences expressing plans for that career, ensuring proper use of future tense and modals. Example: "For a lawyer, I want to help justice. I will need to study law. I would like to gain experience in court."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3 (Pair Writing & Peer Check):</b> Students are paired. Each student writes three sentences about *their own* future career plans, using the learned structures. Then, they exchange papers and check their partner's sentences for correct grammar, vocabulary, and clarity, making light corrections or suggestions. (e.g., "Good use of 'want to', but check spelling of 'professional'.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Future Careers"</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual written product (short narrative).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> Students will write a short narrative (1-2 paragraphs, 6-8 sentences) about their personal future career plans, similar to Leo's story. They must:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">State the career they "want to be."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Explain their "motivation" (why they want to be that).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">List at least two "planned steps" (e.g., "First, I will...", "Next, I would like to...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Incorporate at least 3-4 target vocabulary words (e.g., goals, train, achieve, skilled, important, professional).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use Wh-questions (from the prompt) to guide their thinking (e.g., "What do you want to be in the future?", "Why do you want to choose this career?", "What steps will you take to achieve your goals?").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher circulates, providing support and reminding students to express intentions using "I plan to..." and "I would like to..."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Formative assessment strategy</i></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Peer Review of narratives. Students exchange their written narratives from Stage 4 with a new partner. Each student reads their partner's narrative and provides written feedback using a simple checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (on checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Includes chosen career (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">States motivation (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Lists at least two steps (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses "want to + infinitive" correctly (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses future tense (will/plan to) correctly (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses at least 3 vocabulary words correctly (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Overall clarity (Good/Okay/Needs work)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><i>Space for written comment:</i> "Good job describing your future goals!" or "I suggest you add more details about..."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students reflect on their own writing and the feedback received by answering:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing I wrote well in my narrative?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing I could improve in my writing next time?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-8 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did giving feedback to my classmate help me understand how to write better about career plans?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing about my future goals (motivation or steps) was easiest/most difficult?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., students effectively used "want to + infinitive," peer review was engaging).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next lesson (Lesson 5 - Mediation & Integration), especially regarding writing clarity or vocabulary usage? (e.g., providing more sentence starters, focusing on paragraph organization).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Mediation & Integration), students will summarize their career plans and perhaps create a visual aid or present it orally, integrating the writing they practiced today into a broader project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-4 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>